  "text": "Let the five positive integers be \\(a, a+d, a+2d, a+3d, \\) and \\(a+k\\). Since the first four terms form a harmonic progression, the reciprocals of these terms form an arithmetic progression. So we have the following relationships:\n\n1. \\( \\frac{1}{a} - \\frac{1}{a+d} = \\frac{1}{a+d} - \\frac{1}{a+2d} \\)\n2. \\( \\frac{1}{a+d} - \\frac{1}{a+2d} = \\frac{1}{a+2d} - \\frac{1}{a+3d} \\)\n3. \\( \\frac{1}{a+2d} - \\frac{1}{a+3d} = \\frac{1}{a+3d} - \\frac{1}{a+k} \\)\n\nBetween terms \\(a\\) and \\(a+3d\\), the difference is \\(3d\\). Between terms \\(a+3d\\) and \\(a+k\\), the difference is \\(k-3d\\). The difference between the first and last terms is 24, so \\(k-a = 24\\). Since the last four terms form an arithmetic progression, the difference between consecutive terms must be the same. This gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{a+d} - \\frac{1}{a+2d} = \\frac{1}{a+3d} - \\frac{1}{a+4d}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we simplify the harmonic progression condition:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{a+d} - \\frac{1}{a+2d} = \\frac{1}{a+2d} - \\frac{1}{a+3d}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by \\((a+d)(a+2d)(a+3d)\\) gives:\n\n\\[\n(a+3d) - (a+2d) = (a+2d) - (a+d)\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nd = d\n\\]\n\nThis is an identity and doesn't give us new information. However, it confirms that the relationship is correct. Now we use the arithmetic progression condition. Between terms \\(a\\) and \\(a+k-3d\\), the difference is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{a+3d} - \\frac{1}{a+4d} = \\frac{1}{a+k-3d} - \\frac{1}{a+k}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by \\((a+3d)(a+4d)(a+k)\\) gives:\n\n\\[\n(a+k) - (a+3d) = (a+4d) - (a+k-3d)\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nk - 3d = 4d - k + 3d\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this gives:\n\n\\[\nk - 3d = 4d - k + 3d\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\n2k = 7d\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{7d}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow we know that \\(k = a + 3d\\) and \\(k = \\frac{7d}{2}\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\na + 3d = \\frac{7d}{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2a + 6d = 7d\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2a = d\n\\]\n\nSince \\(k = \\frac{7d}{2}\\) and \\(k = a + 3d\\) and we know \\(k - a = 24\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{7d}{2} - d = 24\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{7d - 2d}{2} = 24\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5d}{2} = 24\n\\]\n\n\\[\n5d = 48\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{48}{5}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(d = \\frac{48}{5}\\) into \\(2a = d\\):\n\n\\[\n2a = \\frac{48}{5}\n\\]\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{24}{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we can find \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\nk = a + 3d\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{24}{5} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{48}{5}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{144}{5}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{168}{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we have the five terms as:\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{24}{5}, \\quad a+d = \\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{48}{5} = \\frac{72}{5}, \\quad a+2d = \\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{96}{5} = \\frac{120}{5}, \\quad a+3d = \\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{144}{5} = \\frac{168}{5}, \\quad a+k = \\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{168}{5} = \\frac{192}{5}\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the five terms is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24}{5} + \\frac{72}{5} + \\frac{120}{5} + \\frac{168}{5} + \\frac{192}{5} = \\frac{720}{5} = 144\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{144}\n\\]",
